An '''Artist''' (Japanese: '''{{ruby|芸術家|げいじゅつか}}''' ''Artist'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in the [[Generation IV]] {{pkmn|games}}. They are most commonly depicted as old men wearing berets and carrying art supplies. They are similar to the {{tc|Painter}} class from {{game|FireRed and LeafGreen|s}}. In Generation IV, they use Pokémon that can learn {{m|Copycat}} and {{m|Mimic}}, such as {{p|Bonsly}} and {{p|Mime Jr.}}, as well as Pokémon related to the arts, such as {{p|Kricketune}} and {{p|Smeargle}}.

In [[Generation V]]'s [[Battle Subway]], some of them specialize in Pokémon resembling decorative art, with many of these being {{type|Steel}} Pokémon.

In [[Generation VI]], female Artists, depicted as young women holding a paintbrush covered in paint, were introduced. Similar to [[Generation III]]'s Painters, Artists exclusively use {{p|Smeargle}}. In [[Double Battle]]s, two Artists, one male and female, form an {{tc|Artist Family}}. 

In [[Pokémon Sword and Shield]], Artists are depicted as deranged men holding clay sculptures. They keep their Pokémon in [[Great Ball]]s. In the {{gal|Battle Tower}}, Artists specialize in a mix of {{type|Fairy}} Pokémon and Pokémon that benefit from {{m|Trick Room}}.

In [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]], Artists are depicted as young female graffiti artists wearing gas masks.

